From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net airoha offload without flow stats when the NPU refuses them

airoha_ppe_offload_setup() failed the whole flow offload setup when the
NPU refused the flow stats area (npu->ops.ppe_init_stats()), so a
missing counter feature cost the hardware offload itself.  Log it once
and go on without stats: a flag makes airoha_ppe_get_total_num_stats_entries()
report none from then on, and every stats path (reset, update on commit,
the reads for the flowtable) already checks that number, so the area the
NPU did not take is never touched.  The SRAM layout programmed by
airoha_ppe_hw_init() still reserves the stats entries, as the NPU was set
up with them.  The stats read path keeps reporting its errors as before.

Generic on purpose: only SoCs whose NPU runs the PPE reach this code (on
AN7563 the host runs the PPE and has no flow stats), and for them the
change is only that offload keeps working with the counters at 0 instead
of not working at all.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -666,6 +666,8 @@ struct airoha_ppe {
 
 	struct airoha_foe_stats *foe_stats;
 	dma_addr_t foe_stats_dma;
+	/* the NPU did not take the flow stats area: offload runs without */
+	bool stats_off;
 
 	/* PPE configured by the host, without the NPU (soc->ppe_host) */
 	bool host_ready;
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -155,6 +155,9 @@ static int airoha_ppe_get_total_num_stat
 {
 	int num_stats = airoha_ppe_get_num_stats_entries(ppe);
 
+	if (ppe->stats_off)
+		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
 	if (num_stats > 0) {
 		struct airoha_eth *eth = ppe->eth;
 
@@ -1711,8 +1714,18 @@ static int airoha_ppe_offload_setup(stru
 	if (ppe_num_stats_entries > 0) {
 		err = npu->ops.ppe_init_stats(npu, ppe->foe_stats_dma,
 					      ppe_num_stats_entries);
-		if (err)
-			goto error_npu_put;
+		/*
+		 * Offload without the flow counters rather than none at all:
+		 * every stats path checks the number of stats entries, which
+		 * is none from here on, so the area the NPU did not take is
+		 * never read or written.
+		 */
+		if (err) {
+			dev_warn(eth->dev,
+				 "NPU flow stats unavailable (%d), offload without\n",
+				 err);
+			ppe->stats_off = true;
+		}
 	}
 
 	airoha_ppe_hw_init(ppe);
